    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "land. My father's never had a vote for mayor in his life. And it was kind of a very idyllic upbringing. Family there for generations. My father's family had been there since the late 19th century. Tennessee, most immediately. My mother's family had been in eastern Arkansas in a similar community and they had met at the University of Arkansas. You know, I had a grandmother and a great aunt there, and both of those of my great aunt didn't have any children or grandchildren of her own, so we were kind of like her children and grandchildren spent summer months with them. You know, you get on your bike in the morning, they could turn you out and be confident you'd make it back safe in the evening, and if you did anything wrong during the day that your neighbors or friends or church members or what have you would. would report back to you. You figured that out pretty quickly as well. And my parents are just great salt to the Earth people. You know, my father's here. All Democrats. All Democrats, yeah, pretty much everyone was in those days. And to this day, there's a lot of counties in Arkansas where if you want to vote for your county judge or your sheriff or your JP, you have to vote in the Democratic primary. That's changing to agree, but it's still the case in many counties. That said, they were all very conservative too. I didn't grow up in a political family. My father was very civic minded. He coached little league. He helped get lights for the field. He's in the Rotary Club. He's been the voice of Dardner Sandler at football for 30 years now, but not politically active. No bumper stickers, no yard signs, in part because all politics was Democratic Party primary politics, so it was mostly personality based. I didn't want to offend the other person. So I didn't grow up in a political household, a conservative in the sense of like a William F. Buckley conservative movement household, but it was a very conservative household in the sense of a traditional household. Like I had to go work on the farm from the time I was five. I had to try to earn my own key, you know, taught, you know, traditional upbringing about differences between right and wrong and personal responsibility and individual initiative and so forth.",
