    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, he was. I mean, I guess I didn't know that there was something other. Someone could be governor other than Bill Clinton until he got elected president. But he was elected attorney general a few months before I was born the governor about a year after I was born, except for a two year period in the early 1980s, who's either governor or president for my entire life until I was 24. Um, and again, you know, all those races are primarily about the, uh, the primary in those days. Uh, but you know, he'd come to our home county, y'all county lied. He'd be at the y'all county fair. There's pictures of me and my Arkansas razorback shirt. I'm four years old with my sister, uh, with Bill Clinton standing behind us. I'm much",
