    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, he was a really great politician, you know, probably one of the best on the campaign trail. Interestingly, you know, I think another great politician came from Arkansas, Mike Huckabee, incredibly skilled, gifted campaigner and communicator. They also from Hope, Arkansas. You know, Bill Clinton grew up more in Hot Springs than in Hope. It doesn't sound as good in the campaign video, but after about six months of his life, I still believe in a place called Hot Springs is not as good a speed. But, you know, they both grew up in rural Arkansas around, you know, people who work with their hands and work on their feet. You know, my cuckity had the added, you know, perspective of being a Baptist preacher and having to deal with all the problems that any preacher has to deal with. But I think that that gave both of them the kind of common touch and the feel on the campaign trail that made them so successful, that helped make Bill Clinton president. came close to making John, Mike Huckabee, our Republican nominee in 2008. Did you learn anything as a politician from watching those guys? You know, I learned a lot of the things at the point that you've made in your book or in your comments that, you know, when you're in campaigns, you have to speak to the common concerns of the voters in a place like Arkansas. Those concerns are making ends meet, being able to pay the bills at the end of the month and put clothes on your kids back and food on their table. Oftentimes, especially today, is certain communities in New York, in Washington, Silicon Valley get more divorced from that common experience. People forget about that. They forget that an extra 10 bucks on the gas bill or the electricity bill or a few extra bucks on taxes makes a big difference. You've written about that in your",
