    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90472.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 47,
    "turn_text": "Now, that certainly wasn't part of the plan. I left my law practice and joined the Army because of the 9-11 attacks. But when I was in high school, we had a very popular and big junior RTC program. And the retired lieutenant colonel and E7 there were both Vietnam veterans. So I certainly learned a lot from them as well. I think they were both appalled by what had happened in Mogadishu, that we committed to half measures. And as opposed to saying this is not our fight or going all in on it. But my father, you know, we talk a lot about Vietnam, especially when we're out of the farm. You know, we grew up on this cattle farm and from the time I was five or six, I was the farm hand. My mother was able to go home, thankfully, for her. So, you know, all the time, you know, he just, you know, would be in the woods. It might be raining and, you know, helicopter would fly over and he'd talk about reminding him from Vietnam. So I had,",
