    "turn_text": "that. There are certainly lessons to be drawn, both from the decision to go to war, and especially the way the war was waged, but I think given where we were in late 2002 and early 2003, the attack that we had faced, what not only our intelligence services, but pretty much every Western intelligence service believed, I think George Bush made the responsible decision. Now, one lesson we should draw from that is to be more skeptical and probing about intelligence, especially when you're making a decision, go to war and part on that intelligence. And certainly, there are lessons to be drawn about the way the war is conducted in the first three years. But I think looking back on it, giving what was known at the time that George Bush made the responsible decision. The,",
