    "turn_idx": 69,
    "turn_text": "you know, one big debate that's, we're still there, obviously. And one of the reasons is that it is very difficult to, in a place that doesn't have democratic institutions, to install them when there are other deeply rooted rivalries, ethnic divisions, religious divisions and so on. Is that a lesson to be drawn from this that we should be a little more humble in our aspirations about what we can do if the parties on the ground are not willing to do it?",
