    "turn_text": "one reason why even though I wasn't in public office at the time, I did not support the airstrikes in Libya in 2011 because it was pretty clear to me that there was no planning whatsoever for any kind of follow-on stabilization operation nor that we were in the kind of dire straits given the threats that we faced in 2003 from Iraq as that we were in 2011 in Libya. And that's another place that lives on. There's a long after party going on in Libya right now that the United States, especially Europe, is still dealing with. And it's a society that's never had democratic governance. It's never have pluralism. It's still deeply tribal in the way a lot of those countries in that region of the world are.",
