    "turn_idx": 112,
    "turn_text": "States has. But, you see, over the last 10 years, I think, you know, too little focus on Europe by American presidents. And you see that, you know, Europe has struggled a lot over 10 years, in part because, as United States looked to the Middle East, especially under George Bush, and then looked to East Asia under Barack Obama, there wasn't that strong guiding hand in European politics to address some very real challenges that Europe faces, especially in its multilateral institutions like the European Union and the Euro. So I think it'd be better if we continue to play that organizing role, but some of these European leaders are going to have to get over their personal differences or differences in style and manner with our president.",
