    "turn_idx": 195,
    "turn_text": "No, because they ultimately did what I'd counsel them to do from the outset. You know, the House leadership introduced a bill on Monday night and they were going to start voting on it on Wednesday. And I said, they really need to hit pies, take the time to assess all of its implications because health care is a very complicated area of law and not rush through a product that was half baked. Now, there was a lot of drama for two or three weeks there. They ultimately had to pull that bill off of the floor. Congress went into recess, deliberations continued. In the end, they spent about eight or nine weeks on it. In my opinion, what they should have done from the very beginning. The House bill to start, the Senate will rot our own bill. We'll see if we can get 50 votes to pass it. I hope we can, and I hope it improves our health care system.",
