    "turn_idx": 202,
    "turn_text": "so we saw the traditional Medicaid program, which supports the traditional Medicaid populations, which no one disputes need that kind of support the indigent elderly, the disabled, the blind and so forth. Very important programs to help people have say developmental disabilities who are living in, you know, open homes. The expansion population, which oftentimes are able-bodied adults, they are not in that traditional Medicaid fee-for-service program. So the waiver that Arkansas got was to use that pot of money for the expansion population to put that group of people on the insurance market itself. Now, we just modified it to some degree. I say, we, the governor, the legislature, the state of Arkansas, and that moved about 70,000 people off of Medicaid and into market insurance. Well, they'll have different options and they'll have a copay and so forth. That's the kind of flexibility that we should give to my governor and to every other state as well.",
