    "turn_idx": 211,
    "turn_text": "But Medicaid spending on a per-beneficiary basis has been not just below the rate of medical inflation, it's been below the rate of core inflation for many years. We think that if we give governors and legislatures more flexibility, so they'll have more tools than just cutting payments to doctors. that we can even see higher quality care delivered at a better price for Medicaid beneficiaries. I mean, that's one of the core goals that we have of healthcare reform is to give governors more flexibility on Medicaid, give them more tools like managed care, for instance, that is very common in the private insurance market to restrain the rate of growth in Medicaid, but also continue to deliver affordable",
